# Between The Sheets

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Classic

- [ ] 3/4 oz [Cognac]{ ing="cognac" }
- [ ] 3/4 oz [rum]{ ing="rum" }
- [ ] 3/4 oz [Cointreau]{ ing="cointreau" }
- [ ] 3/4 oz fresh [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }

### Ideal

- [ ] 1 oz [Paul Beau VS Cognac]{ ing="paul-beau-vs-cognac" }
- [ ] 1 oz Appleton Estate [Reserve Blend Rum]{ ing="reserve-blend-rum" }
- [ ] 3/4 oz [Pierre Ferrand dry curacao]{ ing="pierre-ferrand-dry-curacao" }
- [ ] 3/4 oz fresh [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [Demerara Gum Syrup]{ ing="demerara-gum-syrup" } (Note: instructions in Cocktail Codex require an immersion circulator - need to find an alternative or try with Cointreau as mentioned in the below note)

## Recipe

1. Shake all ingredients with ice, then strain into a chilled coupe

## Notes

1. Source: Cocktail Codex - SideCar Variant
1. Look for balance with a flavorful Rum and weaker Cognac
1. For the Ideal, if using Cointreau in place of the Pierre Ferrand, may be able to get by without the extra sweetener
